  map.set('specs/request-sign.vectors.json', '{\n  "$comment": "Shared request-signing test vectors for the server and the three native clients (08 BR-ID-09 细则「服务端与三端共用一组签名测试向量」; CI checks every implementation against this file). Signing string = upper-case method + \\"\\\\n\\" + path without scheme or host, including the raw query string after \\"?\\" exactly as sent (same percent-encoding and parameter order; no sorting, decoding or dedup) + \\"\\\\n\\" + X-Timestamp + \\"\\\\n\\" + X-Nonce + \\"\\\\n\\" + lowercase_hex(sha256(raw body bytes)); an empty body hashes the empty string. X-Sign = lowercase_hex(HMAC-SHA256(key, signing string)), where the key is the UTF-8 bytes of install_secret. Fields: note = what the case exercises; method = the signing-string method component as given (not a client API argument that would be upper-cased first); path = the signed path; body_utf8 = the exact body text, encoded as UTF-8 bytes without JSON parsing or reserialization, empty string meaning zero bytes; timestamp = the literal X-Timestamp header value; server_time = the server clock in Unix seconds, injected for the skew check; nonce = the literal X-Nonce header value; install_secret = a test value, prefixed with test-, containing a dot, 16 to 128 characters (openapi RegisterDeviceData), never a real device key; expected_signing_string (valid cases only) = the signing string; expected_sign = the X-Sign; expected_reason (invalid cases only) = the single rule the case breaks. valid_cases pass every check: X-Timestamp is a 10-digit integer, |server_time - timestamp| <= 300 (exactly +300 and -300 are included), X-Nonce is 32 lower-case hex characters, method is upper case, path starts with \\"/\\" and has no scheme or host. invalid_cases each break exactly one rule, with every rule judged independently, and the server answers 10401: time_skew (|server_time - timestamp| > 300; +301 and -301 included), timestamp_format (not exactly 10 digits), nonce_length (not 32 characters), nonce_hex (contains a non-hex character), nonce_case (contains an upper-case letter), method_case (method not upper case), path_domain (path carries a scheme or host; a path starting with \\"//\\" always counts as carrying a host). The skew rule reads the timestamp leniently as a number (surrounding whitespace ignored), so each timestamp_format case either is not a number at all or has a numeric value within 300 s of server_time; for the 9- and 13-digit cases server_time is set to that same number, which is not a realistic clock but keeps the case isolated. Each nonce_length case is lower-case hex, so it breaks neither nonce_hex nor nonce_case. The expected_sign of an invalid case is computed over its fields verbatim: the method is not upper-cased and the path is not stripped of its host. method_case and path_domain are therefore not separate server checks: the server signs the upper-case method and the host-free request path, so such a request fails as a signature mismatch. Field order: never place nonce or any other 32- or 40-character hex field on the line right after install_secret (gitleaks rule cn-hex-secret also inspects the following line); expected_sign is 64 characters and is safe there. Not covered here: X-Device-Id validity (10402), nonce replay within 600 seconds per device_id, and the H5 bridge signing path (BR-ID-32).",\n  "version": 1,\n  "valid_cases": [\n    {\n      "note": "BR-ID-09 example: links open with query and JSON body, server time equals ts",\n      "method": "POST",\n      "path": "/v1/links/abc/open?src=agent",\n      "body_utf8": "{\\"no_rebate\\":false}",\n      "timestamp": "1790661600",\n      "server_time": 1790661600,\n      "nonce": "b5a8f07b9dda63c3f78ed24c341d25b3",\n      "install_secret": "test-only.install.device-a",\n      "expected_signing_string": "POST\\n/v1/links/abc/open?src=agent\\n1790661600\\nb5a8f07b9dda63c3f78ed24c341d25b3\\ne656157d50842895976f927a859fc8658503d498c2decbb994aba12bd18a1c5a",\n      "expected_sign": "5715b672cfc2e52a082392ba4d6997110ae6f9583dc076c6ce8b8df0bc9eeb66"\n    },\n    {\n      "note": "empty body: sha256 of zero bytes (e3b0c442...b855)",\n      "method": "POST",\n      "path": "/v1/links/abc/open",\n      "body_utf8": "",\n      "timestamp": "1790661600",\n      "server_time": 1790661600,\n      "nonce": "815affc86096929c944a8b0d6a79627b",\n      "install_secret": "test-only.install.device-a",\n      "expected_signing_string": "POST\\n/v1/links/abc/open\\n1790661600\\n815affc86096929c944a8b0d6a79627b\\ne3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855",\n      "expected_sign": "2b235155f7b5c27ba65773b1bd043e67cf1ef5569dac05619ce8026af0bbc036"\n    },\n    {\n      "note": "non-ASCII body (CJK, full-width punctuation, 4-byte emoji) hashed as raw UTF-8 bytes; spacing kept, no JSON reserialization",\n      "method": "POST",\n      "path": "/v1/inputs/parse",\n      "body_utf8": "{\\"text\\": \\"复制这段文字打开 凑狸测试商品，¥99 👍\\"}",\n      "timestamp": "1790661600",\n      "server_time": 1790661600,\n      "nonce": "8cc81ffe089dd190b5b8dfdb97fbcbe4",\n      "install_secret": "test-only.install.device-a",\n      "expected_signing_string": "POST\\n/v1/inputs/parse\\n1790661600\\n8cc81ffe089dd190b5b8dfdb97fbcbe4\\nb8175f9465d0d2e3951abe27a75d47d52ed0f7079a280eb71f7ae72e90e126ab",\n      "expected_sign": "8536f2f18d484b9b05d55aee03b68c6eb99cf8a1abb22f88cfa899c44c61fe09"\n    },\n    {\n      "note": "unsorted, percent-encoded query kept as sent: no sorting, no decoding",\n      "method": "POST",\n      "path": "/v1/links/convert?b=2&a=1&c=%E4%B8%AD",\n      "body_utf8": "{\\"url\\":\\"https://example.com/item?id=1\\"}",\n      "timestamp": "1790661600",\n      "server_time": 1790661600,\n      "nonce": "e1d272c45ff3520a4e4c8aedd1ab33d6",\n      "install_secret": "test-only.install.device-b",\n      "expected_signing_string": "POST\\n/v1/links/convert?b=2&a=1&c=%E4%B8%AD\\n1790661600\\ne1d272c45ff3520a4e4c8aedd1ab33d6\\n85820a5732f799cce7ee14e34e7b6df81e4